<title>SINGAPORE: Sri Lanka refinery to restart Feb 24 from shutdown.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka refinery to restart Feb 24 from shutdown.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka's state-owned Ceylon Petroleum Corp (CPC) plans to restart its refinery on February 24 after a routine maintenance shutdown which began on January 15, a CPC source said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The Sapugaskanda refinery, located just north of Colombo, has a capacity of 60,000 barrels per day (bpd).</p>
<p>During the shutdown period, CPC has imported a total of 200,000 tonnes of gas oil, jet fuel and gasoline, the source said.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65-870 3084)</p>
</text>
